---
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import MobilityBlueprintTheme from '../components/MobilityBlueprintTheme.astro';
import atlas from '../data/manufacturing-atlas.json';
import '../styles/mobility-manufacturing.css';
const capabilities = [...new Set(atlas.companies.flatMap(c=>c.capabilities))].sort();
const cities = [...new Set(atlas.companies.map(c=>c.city))].sort();
const cityCounts = cities.map(city=>({city,count:atlas.companies.filter(c=>c.city===city).length}));
const description = 'Public manufacturing capabilities around El Segundo: 23 sourced organizations, approximate 25-mile scope, machining, electronics, fabrication, inspection, additive manufacturing and robotics.';
---
<BlockLayout title="El Segundo Manufacturing Atlas" description={description} hideAds showNetworkStrip={false} alternates={[{type:'application/json',href:'/manufacturing.json',title:'Manufacturing directory data'}]}>
<div class="blueprint">
  <nav class="bp-nav" aria-label="Feature navigation"><a href="/">← PointCast</a><span><a href="/mobility-2030/">Mobility 2030 ↗</a><a href="/manufacturing.json">Directory JSON</a><MobilityBlueprintTheme/></span></nav>
  <header class="bp-hero"><p class="bp-kicker">CH.ESC / Regional capability survey / Checked {atlas.checkedDate}</p><h1>What can we<br/>make around here?</h1><p class="bp-intro">A public manufacturing atlas for the El Segundo region: precision machining, electronics, forming, additive manufacture, automation and the people who teach it.</p><p class="bp-notice">{atlas.companies.length} researched organizations. Approximate 25-mile scope; distances are coarse editorial estimates, not geocoded measurements. One near-boundary research entry requires verification. No supplier commitments or flight-qualified capabilities are implied.</p></header>
  <figure class="bp-plate"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="factory-graphic-title factory-graphic-desc"><title id="factory-graphic-title">A regional manufacturing workflow</title><desc id="factory-graphic-desc">Requirements connect to prototype, process, inspection and service. Supporting capabilities include machining, materials, electronics and automation. This schematic illustrates relationships, not a geographic map.</desc><defs><pattern id="factory-grid" width="25" height="25" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M25 0H0V25" stroke="#9ac8ff" stroke-opacity=".15" fill="none"/></pattern></defs><rect width="1000" height="330" fill="url(#factory-grid)"/><g fill="none" stroke="#b8d9ff" stroke-width="2"><path d="M190 115H240M400 115H450M610 115H660M820 115H860M320 160V230H740V160"/><rect x="30" y="65" width="160" height="100"/><rect x="240" y="65" width="160" height="100"/><rect x="450" y="65" width="160" height="100"/><rect x="660" y="65" width="160" height="100"/><rect x="860" y="65" width="110" height="100"/></g><g fill="#e3f1ff" font-family="monospace" font-size="18"><text x="48" y="107">REQUIRE</text><text x="48" y="138">define</text><text x="258" y="107">PROTOTYPE</text><text x="258" y="138">learn</text><text x="468" y="107">PROCESS</text><text x="468" y="138">repeat</text><text x="678" y="107">INSPECT</text><text x="678" y="138">verify</text><text x="873" y="107">SERVE</text><text x="873" y="138">repair</text><text x="280" y="268">MACHINING · MATERIALS · ELECTRONICS · AUTOMATION</text></g><text x="30" y="308" fill="#a9d1ff" font-family="monospace" font-size="14">CAPABILITY ≠ CAPACITY ≠ QUALIFICATION ≠ PROJECT ACCEPTANCE</text></svg><div class="bp-mobile-flow" aria-hidden="true"><span>Define requirements</span><span>↓ Prototype & learn</span><span>↓ Process & repeat</span><span>↓ Inspect & verify</span><span>↓ Service & repair</span><small>Capability ≠ capacity ≠ qualification</small></div><figcaption>BP.M01 / Capability network, not a geographic map or facility plan. Requirements → prototype → process → inspect → service. Every supplier interface needs confirmation.</figcaption></figure>
  <nav class="bp-tabs" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#directory">Capability directory</a><a href="#geography">Regional scope</a><a href="#qualification">Qualify a lead</a><a href="#methodology">Method & updates</a></nav>
  <section class="bp-section" id="directory"><p class="bp-number">01 / Public-source directory</p><h2>Find a capability.<br/>Read the evidence.</h2><p>“Yes” means a public external customer pathway in the stated scope. It may describe product sales, automation solutions or foundry service. It does not confirm available capacity or willingness to take this project. “No” here means no manufacturing service under this directory definition; “unknown” remains unknown.</p>
    <form class="bp-controls" role="search" id="manufacturing-filters" onsubmit="return false"><label>Search organization or process<input type="search" name="query" placeholder="CNC, tooling, electronics…" autocomplete="off" /></label><label>Capability<select name="capability"><option value="">All capabilities</option>{capabilities.map(c=><option value={c}>{c}</option>)}</select></label><label>City<select name="city"><option value="">All cities</option>{cities.map(c=><option value={c}>{c}</option>)}</select></label><label>Outside-work evidence<select name="availability"><option value="">All statuses</option><option value="yes">Yes / public pathway</option><option value="no">No / manufacturing</option><option value="unknown">Unknown</option></select></label><label>Geography<select name="geography"><option value="">All researched candidates</option><option value="approximate-within-radius">Approximate regional scope</option><option value="boundary-check-required">Boundary check required</option></select></label><button type="reset">Reset filters</button></form>
    <p class="bp-count" id="manufacturing-count" aria-live="polite">{atlas.companies.length} records · 0 geocoded boundary confirmations</p><noscript><p class="bp-notice">The full directory is shown below. Search filters need JavaScript; all source links and records remain readable.</p></noscript>
    <div class="bp-grid" id="manufacturing-companies">{atlas.companies.map(c=><article class="bp-card bp-company" data-company-id={c.id}><p class="bp-number">{c.id} / {c.kind}</p><h3>{c.name}</h3><p class="bp-distance">{c.city} · ≈{c.distanceMiles} straight-line miles · ± roughly 2 mi</p>{c.geographyStatus==='boundary-check-required'&&<p class="bp-notice">Near-boundary research context. Exact 25-mile inclusion unverified.</p>}<div class="bp-tags">{c.capabilities.map(tag=><span class="bp-tag">{tag}</span>)}</div><p>{c.summary}</p><dl><dt>Outside work / {c.outsideWork}</dt><dd>{c.availabilityEvidence}</dd><dt>Public location</dt><dd>{c.address}</dd></dl><p class="bp-small">{c.caveat}</p><details><summary class="bp-small">Source & distance record</summary><p class="bp-small">{c.distanceBasis}</p>{c.sources.map((s,i)=><a class="bp-source bp-small" href={s.url}>{s.label} {i+1} ↗ · checked {s.checkedDate}{'linkCheck' in s ? ' · automated check unavailable' : ''}</a>)}</details></article>)}</div><p class="bp-empty" id="manufacturing-empty" hidden>No records match these filters. Try another capability, city or evidence status.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="bp-section" id="geography"><p class="bp-number">02 / Scope without false precision</p><h2>A region, not invented pins.</h2><p>Origin: {atlas.origin}. {atlas.methodology} Coordinates remain null. These city groups are a directory index, not a spatial layout or a driving-distance map.</p><div class="bp-grid three">{cityCounts.map(c=><article class="bp-card"><p class="bp-number">Regional index / {c.count} records</p><h3>{c.city}</h3><p class="bp-small">Read the address and distance basis in each profile. Every estimate needs geocoding before strict radius-based decisions.</p></article>)}</div><p class="bp-small">CSULB is retained as a separately labeled boundary-check research lead. It is not counted as confirmed within 25 miles. None of the entries has a geocoded boundary confirmation in this edition.</p></section>
  <section class="bp-section" id="qualification"><p class="bp-number">03 / From directory to qualified lead</p><h2>The next conversation is specific.</h2><div class="bp-grid"><article class="bp-card"><h3>Match the work package.</h3><p>For nonflight mockups, investigate machining, foam, tooling and polymer processes. Electronics assembly, robotic finishing and independent inspection are distinct supplier scopes. An aerospace OEM nearby does not imply access to its factory.</p><p>Product sourcing differs from contract fabrication. A university research lab differs from an open commercial shop. Read the evidence before asking for work.</p></article><article class="bp-card"><h3>Verify before spending.</h3><ol class="bp-list"><li>Confirm the present address, actual process site, civil-project eligibility and capacity.</li><li>Request current quality scope, traceability, first-article and inspection evidence.</li><li>Agree authorized drawing scope, IP and data handling before transfer.</li><li>Compare written quotes, tooling ownership, quantities, acceptance criteria and lead time.</li><li>Review representative nonflight samples before any safety-critical decision.</li></ol><p class="bp-small">A website logo or quality certificate does not approve a flight-critical part or complete aircraft.</p></article></div><p><a href="/mobility-2030/#factory">See how this region fits a proposed 2030 mobility studio →</a></p></section>
  <section class="bp-section" id="methodology"><p class="bp-number">04 / Evidence maintenance</p><h2>A directory that can be repaired.</h2><p>Curated public-source research checked {atlas.checkedDate}; not an exhaustive manufacturing census. {atlas.verificationWarning} Primary company pages carry the capability evidence. Public city records or company-distributed releases supply selected corroboration; individual caveats preserve failures and stale-address concerns.</p><div class="bp-grid"><article class="bp-card"><h3>Update procedure</h3><p>Recheck the company's current capability and contact pages. Retain the source URL and checked date, confirm process location, and classify outside-work evidence independently. Record a withdrawn or unverified claim as unknown rather than retaining a confident yes.</p><p>Geocode only verified public addresses against the declared origin, retain the method, and flag entries whose uncertainty crosses the radius. Do not invent coordinates, facility interiors or visitor access.</p></article><article class="bp-card"><h3>Machine-readable record</h3><p>Each profile carries a stable ID, capability tags, public location, coarse distance method, explicit outside-work evidence, source links, checked date and caveat. The JSON retains geography status and null coordinates.</p><p><a href="/manufacturing.json">Open /manufacturing.json →</a> · <a href="/mobility-2030-research/manufacturing-directory.csv">CSV directory</a> · <a href="/mobility-2030-research/manufacturing-atlas-brief.md">Full research brief</a></p><p class="bp-small">Corrections can be proposed through the PointCast repository with the record ID, supporting public source and checked date. No contact form or data collection is added here.</p></article></div></section>
  <footer class="bp-footer">PointCast / El Segundo Manufacturing Atlas · Checked {atlas.checkedDate}<br/>Public capabilities only. No endorsement, partnership, available capacity or airworthiness certification. <a href="/mobility-2030/">Mobility 2030</a> · <a href="/">PointCast</a></footer>
</div>
</BlockLayout>
<script>
import atlas from '../data/manufacturing-atlas.json';
import { filterCompanies } from '../lib/manufacturing-atlas.mjs';
function setupManufacturing(){
 const form=document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#manufacturing-filters');
 if(!form || form.dataset.bound)return;
 form.dataset.bound='true';
 const apply=()=>{const values=Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form));const selected=filterCompanies(atlas.companies,values);const ids=new Set(selected.map(c=>c.id));document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-company-id]').forEach(card=>card.hidden=!ids.has(card.dataset.companyId));document.querySelector('#manufacturing-count')!.textContent=`${selected.length} of ${atlas.companies.length} records · 0 geocoded boundary confirmations`;document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#manufacturing-empty')!.hidden=selected.length>0;};
 form.addEventListener('input',apply);form.addEventListener('change',apply);form.addEventListener('reset',()=>setTimeout(apply,0));
}
setupManufacturing();document.addEventListener('astro:page-load',setupManufacturing);
</script>
